{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-19_13-32-32-dragonboat_raft-real-run && cat draft/update.json && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('research.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(d.get('example'),indent=1)[:3000])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"Fiftieth pass: record the ordering between membership acceptance and the raft layer's own membership maps, which is the hand-off at the centre of the configuration axis. The replicated state machine decides acceptance and then calls node.ApplyConfigChange; that path takes the raft mutex, forwards the change to the peer only when accepted, and always reports the outcome back so the pending-config-change gate on the proposal path is cleared or the change is marked rejected. The membership object used for eligibility decisions and the raft remotes/witnesses therefore change under the same serialised step, after the replicated decision rather than before it.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"node_apply_config_change_order\",\n      \"file\": \"node.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 253,\n      \"end_line\": 293,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"raft_config_change_event\",\n      \"file\": \"internal/raft/raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 1566,\n      \"end_line\": 1586,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@ki_config_apply_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"A config change is applied in two stages under the node's raft mutex: the replicated state machine first admits or rejects it in its membership object, then node.ApplyConfigChange forwards the accepted change to the raft peer, which adds or removes the node in its remotes, observers or witnesses and clears the pending-config-change gate; a rejected change skips the peer mutation but still calls RejectConfigChange so the gate is cleared. The node registry is updated in the same call, and a removal of the local node also removes the cluster from the registry and requests local removal.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"A committed ConfigChangeEntry is applied by the state machine while the node is running and the change type is one of AddNode, RemoveNode, AddObserver or AddWitness.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"node_apply_config_change_order\",\n        \"raft_config_change_event\",\n        \"membership_handle_config_change\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n \"rationale\": \"Investigate a sourced local uncertainty\",\n \"sources\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"source\",\n   \"file\": \"REPLACE_WITH_CAPTURED_FILE\",\n   \"start_line\": 1,\n   \"end_line\": 1,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  }\n ],\n \"investigations\": [\n  {\n   \"ref\": \"@question\",\n   \"question\": \"Which applicable caller condition establishes this result?\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"source\"\n   ],\n   \"discriminator\": \"Trace the actual producer and the enclosing protection\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
